205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Crowd control is a public security practice in which large crowds are dispersed to prevent stampedes, fights, brawls involving drunk or unruly individuals, or riots. Stampedes, in particular, can cause hundreds of deaths.[1] Effective crowd management concerns the management of both anticipated and unanticipated crowd events.[12] Crowd control can involve private security guards as well as police officers. Crowd control is often used at large public gatherings such as street fairs, music festivals, stadiums, and public demonstrations. At some events, security guards and police use metal detectors and sniffer dogs to prevent weapons and drugs from being brought onto the venue.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
